1
00:00:01,300 --> 00:00:02,467
<i>The crime rate in the country
is getting worse and worse.</i>

2
00:00:02,600 --> 00:00:06,067
<i>The police are protecting
the criminals and syndicates.</i>

3
00:00:06,433 --> 00:00:08,500
<i> What's in that? I want to see.</i>

4
00:00:08,633 --> 00:00:09,633
<i> Run, fast!</i>

5
00:00:09,767 --> 00:00:10,867
<i> Isn't that in Bolagos?</i>

6
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:12,667
<i>Put that video on the feed.
We're going live.</i>

7
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:13,700
<i> Who are the police chasing?</i>

8
00:00:13,833 --> 00:00:15,633
<i>What's in the truck they're
carrying?</i>

9
00:00:15,767 --> 00:00:17,067
<i> Why did it get to that point?</i>

10
00:00:17,200 --> 00:00:19,033
<i>I'm still here
at Bolagos National High School</i>

11
00:00:19,167 --> 00:00:21,833
<i>where the awarding ceremony
was disrupted.</i>

12
00:00:21,967 --> 00:00:23,200
<i> Don't involve the kid.</i>

13
00:00:23,333 --> 00:00:24,667
<i> I'm not afraid of you!</i>

14
00:00:24,800 --> 00:00:27,333
<i> My father said, never say die!</i>

15
00:00:27,467 --> 00:00:28,467
<i> Never say die.</i>

16
00:00:31,600 --> 00:00:34,033
<i>How did you know there
was this kind of drug transport?</i>

17
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:36,400
<i>We're repacking shabu,
not pillows.</i>

18
00:00:36,533 --> 00:00:38,267
<i>You seem to want to say
I'm an accomplice here.</i>

19
00:00:38,400 --> 00:00:39,567
<i> Are you involved?</i>

20
00:00:39,700 --> 00:00:41,533
<i>I thought we were paying
the officer at the checkpoint?</i>

21
00:00:41,667 --> 00:00:42,567
<i> Ramon is on the payroll.</i>

22
00:00:42,700 --> 00:00:44,633
<i>The one who isn't is that pest
Delgado.</i>

23
00:00:44,767 --> 00:00:46,633
<i>Why don't we just have him
killed?</i>

24
00:00:46,767 --> 00:00:49,033
<i> Your job is to find Ramon.</i>

25
00:00:49,167 --> 00:00:51,133
<i>Believe me, Ma'am,
I won't run away.</i>

26
00:00:52,733 --> 00:00:54,067
<i> Lloyd, check what that is.</i>

27
00:02:34,867 --> 00:02:35,667
Golda.

28
00:02:47,567 --> 00:02:48,467
Golda?

29
00:03:46,233 --> 00:03:49,000
Mother, open the door.

30
00:03:53,833 --> 00:03:55,000
Let's go to the warehouse.

31
00:04:25,400 --> 00:04:26,200
That's enough.

32
00:04:27,567 --> 00:04:29,067
I almost shot you.

33
00:04:30,167 --> 00:04:32,500
You're pretending,
but you want it too, right?

34
00:04:33,833 --> 00:04:34,800
What?

35
00:04:35,167 --> 00:04:38,900
I don't even have a thank-you
gift for the tip I gave you?

36
00:04:39,767 --> 00:04:40,400
A gift?

37
00:04:41,767 --> 00:04:43,767
You should be the one
thanking me

38
00:04:44,300 --> 00:04:46,033
because I'm doing you a favor.

39
00:04:47,600 --> 00:04:49,467
I mean, it's unfair.

40
00:04:50,700 --> 00:04:55,167
The selling of drugs over my
wellness spa is only small time.

41
00:04:55,300 --> 00:04:59,267
But the shipment in exchange
for me not going to jail

42
00:04:59,400 --> 00:05:01,567
was worth 800 million pesos.

43
00:05:02,133 --> 00:05:03,300
But you know,

44
00:05:03,933 --> 00:05:05,933
I did enjoy our nightly
rendezvous.

45
00:05:07,033 --> 00:05:10,433
It's just sad
because it'll be over.

46
00:05:11,433 --> 00:05:15,567
So I guess the tip I'm
giving you is enough, right?

47
00:05:19,500 --> 00:05:20,400
Hey!

48
00:05:21,900 --> 00:05:23,767
Whose drugs did we intercept?

49
00:05:25,167 --> 00:05:28,000
Miguel, I told you,
I don't know!

50
00:05:28,967 --> 00:05:29,767
But...

51
00:05:29,900 --> 00:05:30,933
But?

52
00:05:31,333 --> 00:05:32,400
But what?

53
00:05:33,600 --> 00:05:35,933
Do you want me to close down
your spa?

54
00:05:39,267 --> 00:05:40,300
Okay.

55
00:05:42,867 --> 00:05:45,367
When the news about
the drug bust broke.

56
00:05:45,900 --> 00:05:48,167
A name popped up in my contacts.

57
00:05:48,700 --> 00:05:49,833
What name?

58
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:51,800
Who?

59
00:05:55,567 --> 00:05:56,333
Berdugo (Executioner).

60
00:06:13,433 --> 00:06:14,867
Don't act negatively.

61
00:06:30,633 --> 00:06:34,400
Ouch, ouch! It's me, Joey!
It's Peter!

62
00:06:34,933 --> 00:06:35,900
Peter!

63
00:06:36,033 --> 00:06:37,200
Joey, go away, go away.

64
00:07:03,167 --> 00:07:05,000
Why does she look familiar?

65
00:07:31,967 --> 00:07:33,167
Bingo!

66
00:07:45,800 --> 00:07:48,000
Ouch...

67
00:07:48,167 --> 00:07:49,333
Here.

68
00:07:50,167 --> 00:07:51,000
What's that?

69
00:07:51,533 --> 00:07:52,867
I don't need that.

70
00:07:55,433 --> 00:07:56,200
Ouch.

71
00:07:56,333 --> 00:07:57,367
Ouch!

72
00:07:57,500 --> 00:07:59,467
What's your problem?

73
00:07:59,600 --> 00:08:01,433
I'm going to get injured
even more because of you.

74
00:08:01,567 --> 00:08:03,967
You're still pretending,
you're really hurt!

75
00:08:05,233 --> 00:08:06,033
What's your problem?

76
00:08:06,633 --> 00:08:08,900
How did you do that?

77
00:08:09,033 --> 00:08:11,200
My grip on you was so tight,
you still managed to get away.

78
00:08:11,833 --> 00:08:12,933
You're so strong.

79
00:08:13,733 --> 00:08:15,367
Nothing, you're weak.

80
00:08:15,500 --> 00:08:16,267
What's that?

81
00:08:16,400 --> 00:08:17,367
Nothing.

82
00:08:20,033 --> 00:08:22,067
But where did you learn that?

83
00:08:22,233 --> 00:08:23,367
It's like...

84
00:08:23,500 --> 00:08:26,433
it's like you're the sexy female
assassins that I've watched.

85
00:08:26,567 --> 00:08:27,500
So strong.

86
00:08:28,333 --> 00:08:30,367
Taekwondo moves, Boy.

87
00:08:31,100 --> 00:08:33,900
Of course, my father also taught
me self-defense.

88
00:08:34,967 --> 00:08:37,733
Oh yeah, I forgot.
Your Father is a policeman.

89
00:08:38,933 --> 00:08:41,500
So don't you dare kid me
like that again.

90
00:08:41,967 --> 00:08:44,167
Maybe next time,
that's not all you'll get.

91
00:08:44,867 --> 00:08:47,800
Just chill, you're easy!
I just wanted to prank you.

92
00:08:49,133 --> 00:08:50,667
Because when I saw you
on your way home,

93
00:08:50,800 --> 00:08:52,367
you looked really scared.

94
00:09:02,600 --> 00:09:04,733
I witnessed something, Peter.

95
00:09:05,533 --> 00:09:06,333
Witnessed?

96
00:09:07,167 --> 00:09:08,033
What was that?

97
00:09:19,600 --> 00:09:23,500
<i>No, Madam, no!
I really came here to see Parak.</i>

98
00:09:23,633 --> 00:09:25,233
<i>- Really?
- Yes, Madam!</i>

99
00:09:25,367 --> 00:09:27,600
<i>Believe me, Madam!
I won't run away.</i>

100
00:09:44,733 --> 00:09:47,433
Madam, that's enough.
Have mercy.

101
00:09:47,567 --> 00:09:50,633
You were supposed to cover
for us.

102
00:09:50,767 --> 00:09:52,167
You're the contact
at the checkpoint,

103
00:09:52,300 --> 00:09:54,567
yet the shipment still failed.

104
00:09:54,700 --> 00:09:56,033
If you're hiding something,

105
00:09:56,167 --> 00:09:58,967
now is the right chance
to tell us.

106
00:10:01,733 --> 00:10:04,833
Did you tip off Major Delgado?

107
00:10:04,967 --> 00:10:05,833
No, Madam!

108
00:10:05,967 --> 00:10:08,233
I didn't know he was coming,
Madam.

109
00:10:10,067 --> 00:10:11,267
You're tough.

110
00:10:13,367 --> 00:10:13,967
Matias!

111
00:10:14,600 --> 00:10:16,100
You know me, Matias!

112
00:10:16,800 --> 00:10:18,633
I won't double-cross you.

113
00:10:19,533 --> 00:10:22,067
But two shipments have already
been intercepted.

114
00:10:22,367 --> 00:10:24,100
And you're in charge of both.

115
00:10:24,233 --> 00:10:29,300
Believe me, Madam, Matias.
I don't know!

116
00:10:32,300 --> 00:10:33,833
Let's see how tough you are.

117
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:35,367
Let me go!

118
00:10:35,500 --> 00:10:38,300
Is there really no way
to recover the second shipment?

119
00:10:38,433 --> 00:10:39,633
Have mercy.

120
00:10:39,767 --> 00:10:41,433
Parak will try, Madam.

121
00:10:41,567 --> 00:10:43,600
But he's already taking action
to prevent a third shipment

122
00:10:44,167 --> 00:10:45,633
from getting thwarted.

123
00:10:45,767 --> 00:10:47,033
Madam!

124
00:10:47,167 --> 00:10:48,500
Good.

125
00:10:48,633 --> 00:10:51,000
We have another problem.

126
00:10:51,300 --> 00:10:53,133
I'll take care of Ramon.

127
00:10:55,300 --> 00:10:57,067
That's not what I'm talking
about.

128
00:10:58,933 --> 00:10:59,600
This.

129
00:11:00,767 --> 00:11:02,000
Have mercy!

130
00:11:03,300 --> 00:11:04,400
Matias!

131
00:11:04,533 --> 00:11:05,733
Madam!

132
00:11:09,533 --> 00:11:11,267
Are you sure no one saw you?

133
00:11:13,900 --> 00:11:15,767
I didn't notice anyone
chasing me,

134
00:11:15,900 --> 00:11:17,033
so I think I'm safe.

135
00:11:17,167 --> 00:11:19,267
Where did you get this video?

136
00:11:19,400 --> 00:11:21,433
In the alley in Purok Uno.

137
00:11:22,867 --> 00:11:26,267
My uncle and I installed
the CCTV on the main street.

138
00:11:27,467 --> 00:11:29,967
Every corner is covered
by cameras.

139
00:11:32,833 --> 00:11:34,400
Does that mean I was recorded,
too?

140
00:11:34,700 --> 00:11:35,467
Yes!

141
00:11:35,933 --> 00:11:38,633
And they can use
that to identify you, Joey.

142
00:11:46,167 --> 00:11:47,567
The bread is still hot.

143
00:11:47,700 --> 00:11:48,633
Make sure you also eat.

144
00:11:50,233 --> 00:11:51,000
Here you go.

145
00:11:51,133 --> 00:11:53,100
Who's up for some ice cream?

146
00:11:53,233 --> 00:11:55,633
- Uncle Andrew!
- Hello!

147
00:11:55,767 --> 00:11:56,933
Hello.

148
00:11:58,067 --> 00:12:00,133
It's so early, and you're going
to eat ice cream?

149
00:12:00,267 --> 00:12:01,667
What are you thinking?

150
00:12:04,533 --> 00:12:06,000
Manang!

151
00:12:09,500 --> 00:12:12,700
Manang, please put this inside
first, okay?

152
00:12:12,833 --> 00:12:14,667
Set up a plate for Andrew, too.

153
00:12:15,367 --> 00:12:16,800
No need, Manang. It's okay.

154
00:12:17,900 --> 00:12:19,167
I'm still full, Yvette.

155
00:12:20,633 --> 00:12:21,700
Why are you here?

156
00:12:22,533 --> 00:12:23,367
I need your help.

157
00:12:24,433 --> 00:12:25,400
Okay...

158
00:12:25,633 --> 00:12:27,200
Kids, go and eat.

159
00:12:32,733 --> 00:12:33,700
So,

160
00:12:35,233 --> 00:12:36,367
how do you know her?

161
00:12:37,633 --> 00:12:39,433
That's Golda Briones.

162
00:12:39,567 --> 00:12:41,933
She is one of our minor
sponsors.

163
00:12:42,667 --> 00:12:43,300
Why?

164
00:12:44,800 --> 00:12:48,867
Well, she may or may not be
involved in the case

165
00:12:49,033 --> 00:12:50,400
that I am investigating.

166
00:12:51,867 --> 00:12:53,133
Andrew,

167
00:12:53,800 --> 00:12:55,800
what are you investigating?

168
00:12:59,100 --> 00:13:02,100
If you're not fighting
high government officials,

169
00:13:02,233 --> 00:13:03,267
it's the police.

170
00:13:03,933 --> 00:13:05,600
Andrew, you know what happened
to Mom.

171
00:13:07,833 --> 00:13:09,400
You followed in her footsteps.

172
00:13:10,067 --> 00:13:10,700
You know,

173
00:13:11,500 --> 00:13:14,433
Mom is admired for being brave.

174
00:13:14,567 --> 00:13:15,500
She never backed down,

175
00:13:15,633 --> 00:13:17,600
no matter who she was up
against.

176
00:13:18,167 --> 00:13:20,633
But where did that bravery
get her?

177
00:13:24,900 --> 00:13:26,100
Love?

178
00:13:27,367 --> 00:13:28,600
Love?

179
00:13:30,233 --> 00:13:32,233
Where is my uniform?

180
00:13:32,367 --> 00:13:33,967
Here.

181
00:13:34,800 --> 00:13:36,100
It's ironed already.

182
00:13:36,867 --> 00:13:39,333
You don't use your mouth
when looking for things.

183
00:13:40,467 --> 00:13:41,867
Aren't you going to have coffee?

184
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:44,500
No. I'll just get one
at the precinct. I'm in a hurry.

185
00:13:44,633 --> 00:13:45,100
Wait...

186
00:13:45,233 --> 00:13:46,800
you're always like that!

187
00:13:48,267 --> 00:13:50,800
When you go to work,
you're in a hurry,

188
00:13:50,933 --> 00:13:52,467
but when you get home,
you're not.

189
00:13:52,600 --> 00:13:53,833
I didn't even notice

190
00:13:53,967 --> 00:13:55,533
what time you got home last
night.

191
00:13:56,933 --> 00:13:59,600
Love, I have a lot to do
at the office.

192
00:13:59,733 --> 00:14:01,667
Your workload never lessened.

193
00:14:04,667 --> 00:14:09,300
Miguel, I'm also sad, especially
when Joey isn't here.

194
00:14:09,733 --> 00:14:12,267
I'm often alone at home.

195
00:14:13,467 --> 00:14:14,733
Oh my,

196
00:14:15,933 --> 00:14:19,800
Love, I'm sorry.
This case is important.

197
00:14:20,633 --> 00:14:23,267
But I promise you, after this,
we'll go on a date.

198
00:14:23,400 --> 00:14:24,533
I'll take a break
for the whole day,

199
00:14:24,667 --> 00:14:27,100
for the whole week, okay?
That's a promise.

200
00:14:29,367 --> 00:14:31,133
Okay. I'll take a shower first.

201
00:14:31,267 --> 00:14:33,633
Okay, okay, okay.

202
00:14:50,033 --> 00:14:51,267
<i> Hello?</i>

203
00:14:51,400 --> 00:14:54,067
<i>Meet me at the apartment.
I'll be waiting for you.</i>

204
00:15:21,733 --> 00:15:24,167
You should come here often.

205
00:15:24,300 --> 00:15:26,333
Also, eat well.

206
00:15:26,467 --> 00:15:29,367
Every time I see you,
you get thinner and thinner.

207
00:15:30,067 --> 00:15:34,500
Also, why don't you just live
here, so you can eat healthily?

208
00:15:36,200 --> 00:15:38,967
How can your brother live
as a bachelor

209
00:15:39,100 --> 00:15:41,167
if he'll stay under our wing?

210
00:15:42,167 --> 00:15:46,900
He needs his own place where
he can invite his dates over.

211
00:15:47,033 --> 00:15:47,967
Right, Andrew?

212
00:15:49,333 --> 00:15:52,400
Yeah, but I don't have time
for dates, Tomas.

213
00:15:53,200 --> 00:15:57,500
But if investigating a scammer,
a drug addict,

214
00:15:57,767 --> 00:16:01,267
or a rapist counts as dating,
then yeah,

215
00:16:01,400 --> 00:16:02,667
I have plenty of time.

216
00:16:03,400 --> 00:16:05,400
They just can't get into
my room.

217
00:16:06,800 --> 00:16:11,000
And then what about writing
about my feeding programs,

218
00:16:11,167 --> 00:16:13,433
you know, my charity works?

219
00:16:13,567 --> 00:16:18,467
So that I can get more sponsors,
right?

220
00:16:18,600 --> 00:16:20,067
It's a good thing your husband
is a hardworking

221
00:16:20,200 --> 00:16:22,500
and successful businessman,

222
00:16:23,067 --> 00:16:26,900
so he can finance
your NGO projects.

223
00:16:28,233 --> 00:16:29,367
Thank you, Honey.

224
00:16:32,533 --> 00:16:35,633
So, Andrew, what are you working
on right now?

225
00:16:37,133 --> 00:16:38,333
It's a new case.

226
00:16:38,467 --> 00:16:41,733
I'm planning to investigate
the foiled drug transport

227
00:16:41,900 --> 00:16:43,833
that happened in Bolagos.

228
00:16:43,967 --> 00:16:45,367
I have a feeling

229
00:16:45,500 --> 00:16:48,833
that it's not just a small-time
syndicate behind that.

230
00:17:04,567 --> 00:17:06,067
<i> You're going to escape?</i>

231
00:17:06,200 --> 00:17:07,067
<i> No Madam!</i>

232
00:17:07,200 --> 00:17:09,500
<i>Believe me, Madam!
I won't run away.</i>

233
00:17:20,500 --> 00:17:22,033
Hey, Sir. What's that?

234
00:17:22,167 --> 00:17:25,067
We're just going to update
the CCTV in this area.

235
00:17:25,200 --> 00:17:26,267
Update?

236
00:17:26,400 --> 00:17:30,833
Well, it's been updated.
Someone went here this morning.

237
00:17:30,967 --> 00:17:33,400
Girl, it's your time there.

238
00:17:33,533 --> 00:17:36,033
It's a good thing you and your
uncle installed the CCTVs

239
00:17:36,167 --> 00:17:37,167
in purok uno, right?

240
00:17:38,267 --> 00:17:40,000
At least, we got the chip
right away.

241
00:17:44,200 --> 00:17:47,333
Okay, fine! Basic!
It's gone. Safe.

242
00:17:48,200 --> 00:17:48,967
Really?

243
00:17:49,867 --> 00:17:51,633
Okay? As in all of my footage
that was captured,

244
00:17:51,767 --> 00:17:52,767
there's no trace left?

245
00:17:53,400 --> 00:17:54,567
Yeah, yes.

246
00:17:54,700 --> 00:17:57,033
And, yes,
all the data in the Cloud,

247
00:17:57,167 --> 00:17:59,067
it's been erased,
so they can't dig up anything.

248
00:17:59,200 --> 00:18:00,200
We're safe, right?

249
00:18:00,633 --> 00:18:02,433
- Awesome, right?
- You're really awesome!

250
00:18:02,567 --> 00:18:03,967
I'm very impressed with you.

251
00:18:04,100 --> 00:18:06,200
With Peter,
everything is better.

252
00:18:06,333 --> 00:18:07,267
You're welcome.

253
00:18:07,900 --> 00:18:09,100
You're so arrogant.

254
00:18:13,900 --> 00:18:17,167
But what are you planning
to do with the video?

255
00:18:17,300 --> 00:18:18,300
Don't say you're going
to post it,

256
00:18:18,433 --> 00:18:19,400
that's not allowed.

257
00:18:20,633 --> 00:18:21,467
No, of course not.

258
00:18:25,067 --> 00:18:26,500
Well, not yet.

259
00:18:27,300 --> 00:18:29,233
We'll get there, but not now.

260
00:18:29,367 --> 00:18:31,233
Why don't you show it
to your Father?

261
00:18:31,500 --> 00:18:33,067
Maybe not for now.

262
00:18:34,033 --> 00:18:36,333
Father's case is huge.

263
00:18:36,467 --> 00:18:38,400
I don't want to add
to what he's thinking.

264
00:18:45,800 --> 00:18:49,367
Okay, just eat. Don't be shy.
I'll take care of it.

265
00:18:49,500 --> 00:18:51,400
I'll pay for it
if you want to just order.

266
00:18:51,533 --> 00:18:54,400
Your mother asked me
to feed you.

267
00:18:54,533 --> 00:18:56,367
You and Mother are talking,
right?

268
00:18:59,867 --> 00:19:03,767
She often calls me
when you're here in Manila.

269
00:19:03,900 --> 00:19:06,133
Of course, I'm the one
who is close to you, right?

270
00:19:06,800 --> 00:19:10,733
Joey said that you and his
Father are best friends?

271
00:19:10,967 --> 00:19:13,067
No, we're not best friends.

272
00:19:15,400 --> 00:19:17,000
Siblings, yes.

273
00:19:19,500 --> 00:19:20,933
Because that's how it is, Son.

274
00:19:21,267 --> 00:19:23,967
Miguel and I are deeply
connected, right?

275
00:19:25,400 --> 00:19:28,833
We share everything,
and we help each other.

276
00:19:29,000 --> 00:19:29,767
Because inside the Academy,

277
00:19:29,900 --> 00:19:32,833
if you don't have what they call
a buddy,

278
00:19:33,733 --> 00:19:34,767
you won't survive there.

279
00:19:34,900 --> 00:19:38,600
That's why the depth of our
brotherhood developed.

280
00:19:38,733 --> 00:19:40,500
That's why,
now she's my Godchild.

281
00:19:41,400 --> 00:19:43,967
Wow, your connection is
something else, isn't it?

282
00:19:44,100 --> 00:19:47,600
I rarely see that kind of thing
anymore.

283
00:19:47,733 --> 00:19:50,133
That's why I'm telling you, Son,

284
00:19:51,800 --> 00:19:53,467
don't fool around
with my Goddaughter

285
00:19:53,600 --> 00:19:56,700
because you won't only deal
with her father, but also me.

286
00:19:56,833 --> 00:19:59,733
Come on, oh my. Godfather,
he is not my boyfriend.

287
00:19:59,867 --> 00:20:01,400
That's disgusting, yuck.

288
00:20:01,567 --> 00:20:03,333
Wow, wow.

289
00:20:03,467 --> 00:20:05,633
And you thought I was going to
make you my girlfriend?

290
00:20:06,200 --> 00:20:07,767
You don't even take a bath!

291
00:20:09,033 --> 00:20:10,433
Hey!

292
00:20:10,567 --> 00:20:11,800
No, no.

293
00:20:11,933 --> 00:20:14,600
No, just a joke, just a joke.

294
00:20:14,733 --> 00:20:16,133
That's enough.

295
00:20:16,267 --> 00:20:17,467
Eat, go ahead.

296
00:20:17,600 --> 00:20:19,267
That's enough. That's it.

297
00:20:20,633 --> 00:20:22,933
By the way, Joey.

298
00:20:25,300 --> 00:20:31,267
Have you heard anything
about the drug bust in Bolagos?

299
00:20:31,400 --> 00:20:33,033
Have you talked to Father?

300
00:20:34,633 --> 00:20:37,833
No, we just talked about
it at the station.

301
00:20:38,333 --> 00:20:40,700
But I've been trying to call
your Father too.

302
00:20:41,267 --> 00:20:43,433
But he's not answering.
Maybe he's just busy.

303
00:20:46,267 --> 00:20:47,167
Godfather...

304
00:20:47,800 --> 00:20:48,833
actually,

305
00:20:48,967 --> 00:20:53,067
I came to you because I wanted
to ask you something.

306
00:20:53,200 --> 00:20:54,367
About what?

307
00:20:55,933 --> 00:20:56,867
Godfather,

308
00:20:57,267 --> 00:20:59,500
hasn't anyone filed a missing
person report at the station?

309
00:21:00,333 --> 00:21:04,500
Or hasn't anyone found a man's
body in the past few days?

310
00:21:11,733 --> 00:21:14,100
Yes, all of that is effective.

311
00:21:14,233 --> 00:21:16,133
Madam, it's P12,999.

312
00:21:16,267 --> 00:21:17,733
I've had a lot of dark spots
lately.

313
00:21:18,400 --> 00:21:19,567
Oh, my...

314
00:21:23,367 --> 00:21:25,700
What, G, Madam?
Don't think about it.

315
00:21:25,833 --> 00:21:27,167
Your skin might get stressed.

316
00:21:27,300 --> 00:21:28,333
Lizzie!

317
00:21:28,467 --> 00:21:31,200
Lizzie, come on.
Please assist this...

318
00:21:31,333 --> 00:21:33,267
this client of ours, okay?

319
00:21:33,400 --> 00:21:36,600
Hurry, okay? Sure, Madam!

320
00:21:42,867 --> 00:21:44,233
Good evening, Sir.

321
00:21:46,200 --> 00:21:47,233
Good evening.

322
00:21:49,333 --> 00:21:51,367
Do you need any treatment?

323
00:21:52,767 --> 00:21:54,033
Facial?

324
00:21:54,700 --> 00:21:56,267
Body sculpting?

325
00:21:58,567 --> 00:22:00,233
Or...

326
00:22:03,700 --> 00:22:05,267
massage?

327
00:22:07,133 --> 00:22:08,500
That's not on our menu,

328
00:22:08,633 --> 00:22:13,200
but for you,
I would consider it.

329
00:22:13,667 --> 00:22:15,400
I'm just here to ask you
something.

330
00:22:16,933 --> 00:22:19,333
Shoot it, Baby boy.

331
00:22:20,800 --> 00:22:24,667
What's your relationship
with Major Miguel Delgado?

332
00:22:42,000 --> 00:22:44,100
The next batch for shipment
is ready.

333
00:22:44,233 --> 00:22:45,467
I talked to Parak.

334
00:22:45,933 --> 00:22:48,367
He's sure there won't
be any problems.

335
00:22:49,400 --> 00:22:52,967
That's what he said last time,
yet look what happened.

336
00:22:53,200 --> 00:22:56,167
We really have to do something
with that Miguel Delgado.

337
00:22:58,400 --> 00:23:02,033
We've lost money twice
because of that policeman.

338
00:23:02,167 --> 00:23:04,300
We've lost two shipments.

339
00:23:06,233 --> 00:23:08,033
What do you want to happen,
Boss?

340
00:23:08,167 --> 00:23:09,167
We still have Ramon.

341
00:23:09,733 --> 00:23:11,000
We have him alive.

342
00:23:11,133 --> 00:23:12,700
What do you want to do with him?

343
00:23:14,767 --> 00:23:15,633
In chess,

344
00:23:16,633 --> 00:23:18,400
to get your opponent
to come out,

345
00:23:19,933 --> 00:23:21,300
you need a bait.

346
00:23:25,033 --> 00:23:29,467
Use Ramon to get that jerk
Delgado out.

347
00:23:34,167 --> 00:23:35,233
Miguel is a problem.

348
00:23:36,100 --> 00:23:37,467
He's a block in our system.

349
00:23:38,933 --> 00:23:40,333
In chess,

350
00:23:41,367 --> 00:23:42,633
what do you do to the piece

351
00:23:42,767 --> 00:23:43,933
that is an obstacle
in your plan?

352
00:23:53,233 --> 00:23:54,467
You knock it down.

353
00:24:06,833 --> 00:24:08,433
Who really are you, Mister?

354
00:24:08,567 --> 00:24:09,600
And you too, Miss?

355
00:24:09,733 --> 00:24:10,767
My fellow tirada's,

356
00:24:10,900 --> 00:24:14,333
now that Staff Sergeant
Ramon Orbos is dead,

357
00:24:14,467 --> 00:24:16,567
tortured and executed.

358
00:24:16,700 --> 00:24:19,100
He was involved in Father's drug
bust case.

359
00:24:19,233 --> 00:24:21,900
Do you have any idea,
Major, who did this?

360
00:24:22,033 --> 00:24:23,167
Stop investigating.

361
00:24:23,300 --> 00:24:25,000
Mother, I've been calling Father
for a while.

362
00:24:25,133 --> 00:24:26,367
He's not really answering.

363
00:24:26,500 --> 00:24:29,067
You know you can't bother him
at work.

364
00:24:29,233 --> 00:24:31,567
Where were you between 1
and 2 AM last night,

365
00:24:31,700 --> 00:24:32,700
Major Delgado?

366
00:24:32,833 --> 00:24:36,867
Is he really a hero or also
hungry for money?
